The maximum number of family day care educators that may be engaged or registered by the approved provider is 15. The approved provider must identify and maintain an up to date record of this service’s family day care educators operating in a family day care residence or approved family day care venue in Victoria who may be at risk of bushfire (bushfire-at-risk educators); 

For any bushfire-at-risk educators, the approved provider must ensure that: 

bushfire-at-risk educators do not operate on any day declared by the Victorian Emergency Management Commissioner to be a day of ‘Catastrophic” Fire Danger Rating that would apply to the location in which that family day care residence or approve family day care venue is located; and 

the service’s emergency and evacuation policies and procedures required under regulation 168 of the Education and Care Services National Regulations include a current Emergency Management Plan (EMP) for managing the service’s bush-fire related risks; 

the Emergency Management Plan (EMP) is kept up to date, reflects the family day care educator’s operating context and includes: 

procedures for monitoring and managing bushfire risks and events; 

procedures for notifying families of any closure 

the Emergency Management Plan (EMP) is reviewed and updated as necessary at least once each calendar year.  The approved provider must notify the Regulatory Authority within 5 days of the commencement of the operation of the family day care service.  The approved provider within 5 days of the commencement of the operation of the family day care service must submit to the Regulatory Authority: 

a copy of the register of family day care educators, co-ordinators and assistants that complies with section 269 of the Education and Care Services National Law Act 2010 and regulation 153 of the Education and Care Services National Regulations 2011. 

a copy of the record of staff engaged or employed by the family day care service that complies with regulation 154 of the Education and Care Services National Regulations 2011.

